  "title": "Ziyarat of Imam Husayn (a.s.)",
  "data": "Imam Husayn (a.s.)\nPerform ghusl and put on your cleanest clothes.\nAt the gate of the shrine, facing the qiblah, send salutations on the Prophet, Imam Ali, Lady Fatimah, Imam al-Hasan, Imam al-Husayn and the Imams (a.s.) and ask permission to enter, as in [Ziyarat of Imam Husayn (a.s.) on the Day of Arafah](G75).\nEnter, stand at the tomb and recite 100 times:\nاَللّٰهُ اَكْبَرُ\nALLAAHU AKBAR\nAllah is the Most Great.\nThen recite the ziyarat:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O son of Allah's Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ خَاتَمِ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA KHAATAMIN NABIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of the seal of the Prophets.\nالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ سَيِّدِ الْمُرْسَلِينَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA SAYYIDIL MURSALEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of the chief of the Messengers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ سَيِّدِ الْوَصِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA SAYYIDIL WASIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of the chief of the Prophets' successors.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَبَا عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ABAA A'BDILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Aba-'Abdullah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُسَيْنَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUSAYNABNA A'LIYY\nPeace be upon you, O al-Husayn the son of Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ فَاطِمَةَ سَيِّدَةِ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNA FAATIMATA SAYYIDATI NISAA'IL A'ALAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O son of Fatimah the Doyenne of the women of the world.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَلِيَّ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ وَلِيِّهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WALIYYALLAAHI WABNA WALIYYIH\nPeace be upon you, O saint of Allah and son of His saint.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَفِيَّ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ صَفِيِّهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAFIYYALLAAHI WABNA SAFIYYIH\nPeace be upon you, O select of Allah and son of His select.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حُجَّةَ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ حُجَّتِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HUJJATALLAAHI WABNA HUJJATIH\nPeace be upon you, O argument of Allah and son of His argument.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَبِيْبَ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ حَبِيْبِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HABEEBALLAAHI WABNA HABEEBIH\nPeace be upon you, O beloved by Allah and son of the beloved by Him.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا سَفِيْرَ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ سَفِيْرِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAFEERALLAAHI WABNA SAFEERIH\nPeace be upon you, O representative of Allah and son of His representative.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَازِنَ الْكِتَابِ الْمَسْطُوْرِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAAZINAL KITAABIL MASTOOR\nPeace be upon you, O keeper of the inscribed Scripture.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا وَارِثَ التَّوْرَاةِ وَالْاِنْجِيْلِ وَالزَّبُوْرِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA WAARITHAT TAWRAATI WAL INJEELI WAZ ZABOOR\nPeace be upon you, O inheritor of the Torah, the Gospel, and the Psalms.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَمِيْنَ الرَّحْمٰنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AMEENAR RAHMAAN\nPeace be upon you, O trustee of the All-beneficent God.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا شَرِيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SHAREEKAL QUR'AAN\nPeace be upon you, O partner of the Qur'an.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَمُوْدَ الدِّيْنِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'MOODAD DEEN\nPeace be upon you, O support of the religion.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بَابَ حِكْمَةِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA BAABA HIKMATI RABBIL A'ALAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O door to the wisdom of the Lord of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا بَابَ حِطَّةٍ الَّذِيْ مَنْ دَخَلَهٗ كَانَ مِنَ الْاٰمِنِينَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA BAABA HITTATINIL LADHEE MAN DAKHALAHOO KAANA MINAL AAMINEEN\nPeace be upon you, O door of Forgiveness; he who enters from this door will be of the secured ones.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَيْبَةَ عِلْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'YBATA I'LMILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O case of Allah's knowledge.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَوْضِعَ سِرِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAWDI'A SIRRILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O place of Allah's secret.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ثَارَ اللّٰهِ وَابْنَ ثَارِهٖ وَالْوِتْرَ الْمَوْتُوْرَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA THAARALLAAHI WABNA THAARIHEE WAL WITRAL MAWTOOR\nPeace be upon you, O (the object of) Allah's vengeance and the violated sanctity.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلَى الْاَرْوَاحِ الَّتِيْ حَلَّتْ بِفِنَاۤئِكَ وَاَنَاخَتْ بِرَحْلِكَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA WA A'LAL ARWAAHIL LATEE HALLAT BIFINAA'IKA WA ANAAKHAT BIRAHLIK\nPeace be upon you and upon the souls that resided in your yard and settled down near your caravan.\nبِاَبِيۤ اَنْتَ وَاُمِّيْ وَنَفْسِيْ يَاۤ اَبَا عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ\nBI-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE WA NAFSEE YAA ABAA A'BDILLAAH\nMay Allah accept my father, my mother, and myself as ransoms for you, O Aba-'Abdullah.\nلَقَدْ عَظُمَتِ الْمُصِيْبَةُ وَجَلَّتِ الرَّزِيَّةُ بِكَ عَلَيْنَا وَعَلٰى جَمِيْعِ اَهْلِ الْاِسْلَامِ\nLAQAD A'ZUMATIL MUSEEBATU WA JALLATIR RAZIYYATU BIKA A'LAYNAA WA A'LAA JAMEE'I AHLIL ISLAAM\nUnbearable is the sorrow and never-racking is the agony you put up with, for us and for all (true) Muslims.\nفَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ اُمَّةً اَسَّسَتْ اَسَاسَ الظُّلْمِ وَالْجَوْرِ عَلَيْكُمْ اَهْلَ الْبَيْتِ\nFALA'ANALLAAHU UMMATAN ASSASAT ASAASAZ ZULMI WAL JAWRI A'LAYKUM AHLAL BAYT\nCurse of Allah be on the people who laid the basis of wronging and injustice against you the Household of the Prophet.\nوَلَعَنَ اللّٰهُ اُمَّةً دَفَعَتْكُمْ عَنْ مَقَامِكُمْ وَاَزَالَتْكُمْ عَنْ مَرَاتِبِكُمُ الَّتِيْ رَتَّبَكُمُ اللّٰهُ فِيْهَا\nWA LA'ANALLAAHU UMMATAN DAFA'ATKUM A'N MAQAAMIKUM WA AZAALATKUM A'N MARAATIBIKUMUL LATEE RATTABAKUMULLAAHU FEEHAA\nCurse of Allah be upon the people who removed you from your position and took you away from your actual ranks that Allah has chosen for you.\nبِاَبِيْ اَنْتَ وَاُمِّيْ وَنَفْسِيْ يَاۤ اَبَا عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ\nBI-ABEE ANTA WA UMMEE WA NAFSEE YAA ABAA A'BDILLAAH\nMay Allah accept my father, my mother, and me as ransoms for you, O Aba-'Abdullah.\nاَشْهَدُ لَقَدِ اقْشَعَرَّتْ لِدِمَاۤئِكُمْ اَظِلَّةُ الْعَرْشِ مَعَ اَظِلَّةِ الْخَلاۤئِقِ\nASH-HADU LAQADIQ SHA'ARRAT LIDIMAA'IKUM AZILLATUL A'RSHI MA'A AZILLATIL KHALAA'IQ\nI bear witness that the shades of the Divine Throne shared the shades of the creatures in shuddering for the shedding of your blood.\nوَبَكَتْكُمُ السَّمَاۤءُ وَالْاَرْضُ وَسُكَّانُ الْجِنَانِ وَالْبَرِّ وَالْبَحْرِ\nWA BAKATKUMUS SAMAA'U WAL ARDU WA SUKKAANUL JINAANI WAL BARRI WAL BAHR\nThe heavens, the earth, and the inhabitants of the gardens of Paradise, the lands, and the oceans - all those wept for you.\nصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ عَدَدَ مَا فِيْ عِلْمِ اللّٰهِ\nSALLALLAAHU A'LAYKA A'DADA MAA FEE I'LMILLAAH\nMay Allah shower upon you blessings as many as the number of what is there in the knowledge of Allah.\nلَبَّيْكَ دَاعِيَ اللّٰهِ\nLABBAYKA DAA'IYALLAAH\nHere I am at your service, O caller to Allah.\nاِنْ كَانَ لَمْ يُجِبْكَ بَدَنِيْ عِنْدَ اسْتِغَاثَتِكَ وَلِسَانِيْ عِنْدَ اسْتِنْصَارِكَ فَقَدْ اَجَابَكَ قَلْبِيْ وَسَمْعِيْ وَبَصَرِيْ\nIN KAANA LAM YUJIBKA BADANEE I'NDAS TIGHAATHATIKA WA LISAANEE I'NDAS TINSAARIKA FAQAD AJAABAKA QALBEE WA SAM'EE WA BASAREE\nIf my body could not respond to your call when you called for aid and my tongue could not respond to your call for help, then my heart, my hearing, and my sight have verily responded to you.\nسُبْحَانَ رَبِّنَا اِنْ كَانَ وَعْدُ رَبِّنَا لَمَفْعُوْلًا\nSUBHAANA RABBINAA IN KAANA WA'DU RABBINAA LAMAF'OOLAA\nGlory be to our Lord! Most surely, the promise of our Lord was to be fulfilled.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ طُهْرٌ طَاهِرٌ مُطَهَّرٌ مِنْ طُهْرٍ طَاهِرٍ مُطَهَّرٍ\nASH-HADU ANNAKA TUHRUN TAAHIRUN MUTAHHARUN MIN TUHRIN TAAHIRIN MUTAHHAR\nI bear witness that you are pure, immaculate, and purified and you are the offspring of the pure, immaculate, and purified ones.\nطَهُرْتَ وَطَهُرَتْ بِكَ الْبِلَادُ\nTAHURTA WA TAHURAT BIKAL BILAAD\nYou are indeed pure and you are the reason for the purity of the lands.\nوَطَهُرَتْ اَرْضٌ اَنْتَ بِهَا [فِيْهَا] وَطَهُرَ حَرَمُكَ\nWA TAHURAT ARDUN ANTA BIHAA FEEHAA WA TAHURA HARAMUK\nPure is the land where you are and pure is your holy shrine.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ اَمَرْتَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَالْعَدْلِ وَدَعَوْتَ اِلَيْهِمَا\nASH-HADU ANNAKA QAD AMARTA BIL QISTI WAL A'DLI WA DA'AWTA ILAYHIMAA\nI bear witness that you enjoined justice and fairness and you called to them.\nوَاَنَّكَ صَادِقٌ صِدِّيْقٌ، صَدَقْتَ فِيْمَا دَعَوْتَ اِلَيْهِ\nWA ANNAKA SAADIQUN SIDDEEQUN SADAQTA FEEMAA DA'AWTA ILAYH\nAnd you are verily honest and veracious, and you were truthful in that for which you called.\nوَاَنَّكَ ثَارُ اللّٰهِ فِي الْاَرْضِ\nWA ANNAKA THAARULLAAHI FIL ARD\nAnd you are verily (the object of) Allah's vengeance on the earth.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ قَدْ بَلَّغْتَ عَنِ اللّٰهِ وَعَنْ جَدِّكَ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَعَنْ اَبِيْكَ اَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَعَنْ اَخِيْكَ الْحَسَنِ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKA QAD BALLAGHTA A'NILLAAHI WA A'N JADDIKA RASOOLILLAAHI WA A'N ABEEKA AMEERIL MU'MINEENA WA A'N AKHEEKAL HASAN\nAnd I bear witness that you did convey on behalf of Allah, on behalf of your grandfather the Messenger of Allah, on behalf of your father the Commander of the Faithful, and on behalf of your brother al-Hasan.\nوَنَصَحْتَ وَجَاهَدْتَ فِيْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَعَبَدْتَهٗ مُخْلِصًا حَتّٰىۤ اَتَاكَ الْيَقِيْنُ\nWA NASAHTA WA JAAHADTA FEE SABEELILLAAHI WA A'BADTAHOO MUKHLISAN HATTAA ATAAKAL YAQEEN\nAnd you advised and strove in the way of Allah and you served Him sincerely until death came upon you.\nفَجَزَاكَ اللّٰهُ خَيْرَ جَزَاۤءِ السَّابِقِيْنَ\nFAJAZAAKALLAAHU KHAYRA JAZAA'IS SAABIQEEN\nSo, may Allah award you with the best of the rewarding of the foremost (to deeds of goodness).\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكَ وَسَلَّمَ تَسْلِيْمًا\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAYKA WA SALLAMA TASLEEMAA\nAnd may Allah bless and exalt you thoroughly.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, (please) send blessings upon Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَصَلِّ عَلَى الْحُسَيْنِ الْمَظْلُوْمِ الشَّهِيْدِ الرَّشِيْدِ قَتِيْلِ الْعَبَرَاتِ وَاَسِيْرِ الْكُرُبَاتِ\nWA SALLI A'LAL HUSAYNIL MAZLOOMISH SHAHEEDIR RASHEEDI QATEELIL A'BARAATI WA ASEERIL KURUBAAT\nand send blessings upon al-Husayn the wronged, the martyr, the orthodox, the slain one whom is wept heavily, and the object of agonies\nصَلَاةً نَامِيَةً زَاكِيَةً مُبَارَكَةً يَصْعَدُ اَوَّلُهَا وَلَا يَنْفَدُ اٰخِرُهَا\nSALAATAN NAAMIYATAN ZAAKIYATAN MUBAARAKATAN YAS'ADU AWWALUHAA WA LAA YANFADU AAKHIRUHAA\nwith such blessings that are increasing, growing, and sacred; the first of which ascends and the last of which is infinite,\nاَفْضَلَ مَا صَلَّيْتَ عَلٰىۤ اَحَدٍ مِنْ اَوْلَادِ اَنْبِيَاۤئِكَ الْمُرْسَلِيْنَ يَاۤ اِلٰهَ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAFDALA MAA SALLAYTA A'LAA AHADIN MIN AWLAADI ANBIYAA'IKAL MURSALEENA YAA ILAAHAL A'ALAMEEN\nand with the best blessings that You ever sent on any of Your missioned Prophets' sons. O God of the worlds!\nKiss the tomb and lay your right cheek, then your left, on it. Walk around it and kiss it on all four sides.",
  "tabs": [
    "Ali al-Akbar (a.s.)\nGo to the tomb of Ali al-Akbar, the son of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.), stand there and recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا الصِّدِّيْقُ الطَّيِّبُ الزَّكِيُّ الْحَبِيْبُ الْمُقَرَّبُ وَابْنَ رَيْحَانَةِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SIDDEEQUT TAYYIBUZ ZAKIYYUL HABEEBUL MUQARRABU WABNA RAYHAANATI RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O veracious, pure, immaculate, dear, favorite, and son of the basil of Allah's Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ شَهِيْدٍ مُحْتَسِبٍ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA MIN SHAHEEDIN MUHTASIBIN WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon you as you are steadfast martyr. Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you.\nمَا اَكْرَمَ مَقَامَكَ وَاَشْرَفَ مُنْقَلَبَكَ\nMAA AKRAMA MAQAAMAKA WA ASHRAFA MUNQALABAK\nHow noble your position is and how honorable your seat is.\nاَشْهَدُ لَقَدْ شَكَرَ اللّٰهُ سَعْيَكَ وَاَجْزَلَ ثَوَابَكَ وَاَلْحَقَكَ بِالذِّرْوَةِ الْعَالِيَةِ حَيْثُ الشَّرَفُ كُلُّ الشَّرَفِ وَفِي الْغُرَفِ السَّامِيَةِ\nASH-HADU LAQAD SHAKARALLAAHU SA'YAKA WA AJZALA THAWAABAKA WA ALHAQAKA BIDH DHIRWATIL A'ALIYATI HAYTHUSH SHARAFU KULLUSH SHARAFI WA FIL GHURAFIS SAAMIYAH\nI bear witness that Allah thanked you for your efforts, magnified your rewards, and joined you to the exalted summit where there is the entire honor in the elevated chambers.\nكَمَا مَنَّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ قَبْلُ وَجَعَلَكَ مِنْ اَهْلِ الْبَيْتِ الَّذِيْنَ اَذْهَبَ اللّٰهُ عَنْهُمُ الرِّجْسَ وَطَهَّرَهُمْ تَطْهِيْرًا\nKAMAA MANNA A'LAYKA MIN QABLU WA JA'ALAKA MIN AHLIL BAYTIL LADHEENA ADH-HABALLAAHU A'NHUMUR RIJSA WA TAHHARAHUM TAT-HEERAA\nSimilarly, He had bestowed upon you and made you one of the members of the Household of the Prophet from whom Allah removed filth and whom He purified with thorough purification.\nصَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكَ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ وَرِضْوَانُهٗ\nSALAWAATULLAAHI A'LAYKA WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUHOO WA RIDWAANUH\nAllah's blessings, mercy, benedictions, and pleasure be upon you.\nفَاشْفَعْ اَيُّهَا السَّيِّدُ الطَّاهِرُ اِلٰى رَبِّكَ فِيْ حَطِّ الْاَثْقَالِ عَنْ ظَهْرِيْ وَتَخْفِيْفِهَا عَنِّيْ\nFASHFA' AYYUHAS SAYYIDUT TAAHIRU ILAA RABBIKA FEE HATTIL ATHQAALI A'N ZAHREE WA TAKHFEEFIHAA A'NNEE\nSo, O pure master, (please) intercede for me with your Lord so that He may unburden and relieve me from the loads (of sins) that I carry on my back.\nوَارْحَمْ ذُلِّيْ وَخُضُوْعِيْ لَكَ وَلِلسَّيِّدِ اَبِيْكَ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْكُمَا\nWARHAM DHULLEE WA KHUDOO'EE LAKA WA LIS SAYYIDI ABEEKA SALLALLAAHU A'LAYKUMAA\nAnd (please) have mercy upon my humbleness and submission to you and to the master, your father. May Allah bless you both.\nThen lay yourself on the tomb and recite:\nزَادَ اللّٰهُ فِي شَرَفِكُمْ فِي الْاٰخِرَةِ كَمَا شَرَّفَكُمْ فِيْ الدُّنْيَا وَاَسْعَدَكُمْ كَمَاۤ اَسْعَدَ بِكُمْ\nZAADALLAAHU FEE SHARAFIKUM FIL AAKHIRATI KAMAA SHARRAFAKUM FID DUNYAA WA AS'ADAKUM KAMAA AS'ADA BIKUM\nMay Allah increase your honor in the Hereafter in the same way as He honored you in this world and may He bless you in the same way as He blessed others on account of you.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكُمْ اَعْلَامُ الدِّيْنِ وَنُجُوْمُ الْعَالَمِيْنَ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAKUM A'LAAMUD DEENI WA NUJOOMUL A'ALAMEENA WAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nAnd I bear witness that you are the signposts of the religion and the stars of the worlds. Peace and Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you.",
    "The Martyrs\nFace the graves of the martyrs and recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ يَاۤ اَنْصَارَ اللّٰهِ وَاَنْصَارَ رَسُوْلِهٖ وَاَنْصَارَ عَلِيِّ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUM YAA ANSAARALLAAHI WA ANSAARA RASOOLIHEE WA ANSAARA A'LIYYIBNI ABEE TAALIB\nPeace be upon you all, O supporters of Allah supporters of His Messenger, supporters of Ali the son of Abu-Talib\nوَاَنْصَارَ فَاطِمَةَ وَاَنْصَارَ الْحَسَنِ وَالْحُسَيْنِ وَاَنْصَارَ الْاِسْلَامِ\nWA ANSAARA FAATIMATA WA ANSAARAL HASANI WAL HUSAYNI WA ANSAARAL ISLAAM\nsupporters of Fatimah, supporters of al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and supporters of Islam.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكُمْ لَقَدْ نَصَحْتُمْ لِلّٰهِ وَجَاهَدْتُمْ فِيْ سَبِيْلِهٖ\nASH-HADU ANNAKUM LAQAD NASAHTUM LILLAAHI WA JAAHADTUM FEE SABEELIH\nI bear witness that you indeed did sincerely for the sake of Allah and strove sincerely in His way.\nفَجَزَاكُمُ اللّٰهُ عَنِ [مِنَ] الْاِسْلَامِ وَاَهْلِهٖ اَفْضَلَ الْجَزَاۤءِ\nFAJAZAAKUMULLAAHU A'NI MINAL ISLAAMI WA AHLIHEE AFDALAL JAZAA'\nSo, may Allah reward you on behalf of Islam and its people with the best of rewarding.\nفُزْتُمْ وَاللّٰهِ فَوْزًا عَظِيْمًا\nFUZTUM WALLAAHI FAWZAN A'ZEEMAA\nBy Allah I swear, you did win a great success.\nيَاۤ لَيْتَنِيْ كُنْتُ مَعَكُمْ فَاَفُوْزَ فَوْزًا عَظِيْمًا\nYAA LAYTANEE KUNTU MA'AKUM FA-AFOOZA FAWZAN A'ZEEMAA\nI wish I were with you so that I would win a great success.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكُمْ اَحْيَاۤءٌ عِنْدَ رَبِّكُمْ تُرْزَقُوْنَ\nASH-HADU ANNAKUM AHYAA'UN I'NDA RABBIKUM TURZAQOON\nI bear witness that you are alive with your Lord, receiving sustenance.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّكُمُ الشُّهَدَاۤءُ وَالسُّعَدَاۤءُ وَاَنَّكُمُ الْفَاۤئِزُوْنَ فِيْ دَرَجَاتِ الْعُلٰى\nASH-HADU ANNAKUMUSH SHUHADAA'U WAS SU'ADAA'U WA ANNAKUMUL FAA'IZOONA FEE DARAJAATIL U'LAA\nI bear witness that you are the true martyrs and the true happy ones and you are the winners in the most elevated ranks.\nوَالسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهُ\nWAS SALAAMU A'LAYKUM WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace and Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you.\nThen return to the head side of the tomb of Imam al-Husayn (a.s.), pray the two-unit prayer of ziyarat, and pray to Allah for yourself, your parents and your brothers in faith."
  ],
  "merits": "To be recited on the night and day of the 1st of Rajab, the 15th of Rajab, and the 15th of Sha'ban.\n\nImam al-Sadiq (a.s.) is reported to have said, “He who visits al-Husayn (a.s.) on the first of Rajab will have all his sins forgiven by Almighty Allah.”\n\nAbu-Nasr is reported to have narrated that he asked Imam al-Rida (a.s.) about the best times of visiting Imam al-Husayn (a.s.). The Imam (a.s.) answered, “The best times are the fifteenth of Rajab and the fifteenth of Sha'ban.”\n\nAccording to the opinion of Shaykh al-Mufid and Sayyid Ibn Tawus, this form of ziyarat is dedicated to the first day of Rajab and the fifteenth night of Sha'ban. However, al-Shahid added that it is also dedicated to the first night of Rajab, the fifteenth night of it, the fifteenth day of it, and the fifteenth day of Sha'ban. In conclusion, this form of ziyarat is dedicated to six times.\n\nAli al-Akbar and the Martyrs: Shaykh al-Mufid adds these two visits. Sayyid Ibn Tawus has also mentioned a form of ziyarat of Ali al-Akbar (the elder son of Imam al-Husayn) and the other martyrs mentioning them by names."
}
